{
  "id": "L44",
  "subnivel": "A2.2",
  "unidad": 11,
  "titulo": "Me gustaría",
  "explicacion": [
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "**would like** significa «me gustaría» o «quisiera». Es la forma amable de pedir, ofrecer e invitar. La forma corta es **'d like**."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "filas": [
        [
          "Pedir algo",
          "I'd like + sustantivo",
          "I'd like a coffee, please."
        ],
        [
          "Pedir hacer algo",
          "I'd like to + verbo",
          "I'd like to check in."
        ],
        [
          "Ofrecer",
          "Would you like + sustantivo?",
          "Would you like some water?"
        ],
        [
          "Invitar",
          "Would you like to + verbo?",
          "Would you like to come?"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tabla",
      "filas": [
        [
          "Would you like some coffee?",
          "Yes, please.",
          "No, thank you."
        ],
        [
          "Would you like to come?",
          "Yes, I'd love to.",
          "Sorry, I can't."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tip",
      "md": "No confundas: **I like coffee** es un gusto de siempre (me gusta el café). **I'd like a coffee** es lo que quieres ahora (quisiera un café)."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "tip",
      "md": "*I want* no es incorrecto, pero con desconocidos suena brusco. En hoteles, restaurantes y aeropuertos usa *I'd like*."
    },
    {
      "tipo": "texto",
      "md": "En el hotel y el aeropuerto:"
    },
